{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.S5So3GeometricWLambda","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.S5So3GeometricWLambda","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.route_closes_with_rescale_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.route_closes_with_rescale_iff","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L157-L170","doc":"**Fit-trap (declined).**  `Σ y_λ = 0.0318 ≠ 1`, so one *could* rescale the production\nweights `y_λ ↦ c·y_λ`, changing the cluster to `c·v_y` and requiring the geometric ratio\n`r_geom` to satisfy `r_geom·(c·v_y) = μ₃`.  Closure under such a rescale forces `c` to the\nspecific value `c = μ₃/(r_geom · v_y)` — i.e. `c` is **inverted from the target `μ₃`**, a\nfree parameter, hence a FIT.  (Even the *derivation-flavoured* choice \"put both weights on\n`Σ=1`\", `c = 1/Σy_λ ≈ 31.5`, only reaches `r_geom·Σy_λ = 1.506`, a `5 %` miss — and is\nitself an undetermined normalization convention, not a derivation.)  This lemma states\nexactly that dependence (closure ⟺ `c` takes the `μ₃`-determined value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geom_cluster_overshoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geom_cluster_overshoots","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L144-L153","doc":"**The genuine geometric cluster overshoots `μ₃` by ~30× (the honest wall).**  With the\nderived geometric cluster value `c₃(geom) = 14.069 MeV` and target `μ₃ = 0.4708`, the\ncluster is positive (right sign, #4360) and far larger than `μ₃` — a scope-(a) overshoot,\nnot the missing `1.585×`.  (`14.069 = 15.6267/1.1109`, the `S`-corrected sibling value.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geom_route_walls","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geom_route_walls","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L130-L142","doc":"**RESULT (probe, 0-fit): the genuine geometric ratio is `47.37`, the needed is `1.585`\n— the geometric route does NOT close.**  `r_geom = r_raw/S = 52.6226/1.1109 = 47.369`\n(forward-evaluated; `μ₃`, AME, CODATA never inverted).  Stated with the derived value and\nthe needed ratio as explicit hypotheses so `μ₃` sets nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geomRoute_closes_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geomRoute_closes_iff","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L125-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeomRouteCloses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeomRouteCloses","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L119-L123","doc":"**Geometric-route closure predicate.**  The A=3 magnitude closes under the genuine\ngeometric `W^{geom}_λ` re-weight iff the derived ratio `r_geom` equals the needed\n`r* = μ₃/v_y`.  `r_geom` is FIXED by `q₀` + hook-lengths (0 fit); a value chosen to satisfy\nthis would be a FIT and is declined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geom_measure_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geom_measure_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L111-L115","doc":"**C1 — the genuine geometric measure sums to `1`.**  With `D² = Σ_λ d_q²` and the raw\nsum `S = D²/[n]_q!`, the genuine measure `W^{geom}_λ = (d_q²/[n]_q!)/S` has total mass\n`(D²/[n]_q!)/S = 1`.  (Stated as: dividing the raw total `S` by `S` gives `1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geom_ratio_eq_raw_ratio_div_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geom_ratio_eq_raw_ratio_div_sum","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L101-L109","doc":"**Normalization correction of the re-weight ratio.**  Because the genuine geometric\nweight is the raw q-Plancherel weight divided by its sum `S`, the genuine re-weight ratio\nis the sibling's raw ratio divided by `S`:  `r_geom = r_raw / S`.  (Here `r_raw = κ_raw/κ_y`\nand `r_geom = geomCoeff κ_raw S / κ_y`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.geomCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.geomCoeff","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L96-L99","doc":"The genuine Beasley–Witten geometric measure is the sibling's raw q-Plancherel weight\n`W^{raw}_λ = d_q²/[n]_q!` divided by its own sum `S = Σ_λ W^{raw}_λ = D²/[n]_q!`:\n`W^{geom}_λ = W^{raw}_λ / S`.  Its character-sum coefficient is therefore `κ_raw / S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.reweight_is_coefficient_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.reweight_is_coefficient_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Re-weight ratio.**  For two weight systems with character-sums `κ_W`, `κ_y`, the\ncluster ratio is `κ_W / κ_y` — the shared `E₀·h⁴` cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.clusterMag_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.clusterMag_smul","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L79-L83","doc":"**Linearity in the weight.**  Scaling the block-weight system by `s` scales the\ncluster by `s` (`κ_{s·w} = s·κ_w` since `κ` is a linear functional of the weight). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.clusterMag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.clusterMag","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3GeometricWLambda.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The A=3 cluster magnitude at a block-weight character-sum `κ` (the weight's\n`h⁴`-coefficient `κ_w = Σ_λ w_λ |χ_λ|`): `c₃ = E₀ · h⁴ · κ_w`.  Linear in the weight. ","signatureChunk":0}]}